# Firebase web config — optional.
#
# MDX Studio runs entirely on localStorage without any of this. These values
# only enable the cloud features: Google sign-in, Firestore sync and Google
# Drive. Leave them unset and those simply stay switched off.
#
# None of these are secrets. A Firebase web API key is a project identifier
# that ships inside the JavaScript bundle every browser downloads — Google
# documents this. Protect the project with Firestore security rules, an
# HTTP-referrer restriction on the key, and the authorized-domain list.
# See docs/CONFIGURATION.mdx.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own project's values from
# Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → Web app.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=""
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=""
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""
